#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/numpy/basics/dtypes.rst:124
msgid ""
"This rule applies to every integer operator -- ``+``, ``-``, ``*``, ``//``, "
"``%``, ``&``, ``|``, ``^``. Float arrays never overflow (they promote to "
"infinity instead), so the cast trick is only needed in the integer case."
msgstr ""
"Deze regel geldt voor elke integer-operator -- ``+``\\ , ``-``\\ , ``*``\\ ,"
" ``//``\\ , ``%``\\ , ``&``\\ , ``|``\\ , ``^``\\ . Float-arrays lopen nooit"
" over (ze promoveren in plaats daarvan naar oneindig), dus de cast-truc is "
"alleen nodig in het integer-geval."
